2026-08-16T12:53:33Z    [ADI:Revenue] GATE critic: Your “reported FY2025Q3: Revenue | $ 3,623,465 | $ 2,640,068 | $ 6,783,728 | $ 5,063,242” source block mixes bases: $3,623,465 and $2,640,068 are quarterly amounts, while $6,783,728 and $5,063,242 are nine‑month year‑to‑date totals (all presented in USD thousands in ADI filings). If your seasonal_trend input (3,112.9 USDm) was derived from that block, it’s on the wrong basis, which explains the 23% disagreement versus guidance and contaminates the forecast. The submitted 3,929.25 therefore rests on a wrong-basis input for FY2026Q3 revenue.
2026-08-16T12:53:39Z    [DE:Worldwide net sales and revenues] GATE critic: You used -8.6% as the FY2024Q3→FY2025Q3 YoY change, but Deere explicitly reported that worldwide net sales and revenues “decreased 9 percent, to $12.018 billion, for the third quarter of 2025.” That -9% is the reported (USD) basis for the exact metric you’re forecasting. Using -8.6% suggests a basis/series mismatch (e.g., equipment-only or adjusted/CC) and skews the weighted trend you applied to derive 10,614.8 USDm for FY2026Q3.
2026-08-16T12:53:56Z    [HD:Adjusted diluted EPS] GATE critic: The proposed $4.68251 is inconsistent with your stated method: applying +0.05% YoY to the FY2025Q2 adjusted diluted EPS of $4.68 gives $4.68234 (4.68 × 1.0005), not $4.68251. So the submitted figure is overstated relative to your own inputs.
2026-08-16T12:54:09Z    [ADI:Adjusted diluted EPS] GATE critic: The “seasonal_trend” input is on the wrong scale: you used 11.6115 USD/share as a quarterly adjusted diluted EPS candidate for FY2026Q3. ADI’s quarterly adjusted/non‑GAAP EPS has historically been in the low single digits (roughly $1–$4 per quarter), not ~$11; 11.6115 looks like an annual/TTM EPS mistakenly treated as a quarterly figure (or a percent misread as dollars). That mis-scaled input inflated the inter-candidate disagreement to 110% and drove the switch to a weighted median; with a correctly scaled seasonal input, the aggregation rule and resulting estimate would change, so the submitted 3.36905 is not reliable.
2026-08-16T12:54:16Z    [DE:Diluted EPS (GAAP)] GATE critic: Wrong anchor period: you claim “no FY2026Q3 prior-year figure” and base the estimate on FY2024Q3 ($6.29), but the proper comparable prior-year for FY2026Q3 is FY2025Q3 (Deere has reported GAAP diluted EPS for that quarter). Using a two-year extrapolation from 2024Q3 instead of the actual FY2025Q3 prior-year quarter is a fiscal-period mismatch that invalidates the estimate.
2026-08-16T12:54:38Z    [ADI:Adjusted gross margin] GATE critic: Your “mean of last 4 reported levels” is not the last four Q3s relevant to FY2026Q3. You averaged FY2020Q3–FY2023Q3 (69.9, 71.6, 74.1, 72.2), but for a FY2026Q3 forecast the most recent four Q3 prints are FY2022Q3, FY2023Q3, FY2024Q3, and FY2025Q3. You omitted FY2024Q3 and FY2025Q3 entirely, so the 71.95% base is built on stale periods and is not the “last four reported” as claimed. This can be verified against ADI’s FY2024 and FY2025 Q3 filings/press releases for adjusted gross margin.
