2026-08-16T12:54:38Z  [ADI] wrote research\ADI.md
2026-08-16T12:54:44Z    [HD:Comparable sales, total company] GATE critic: Your blend mixes units: the “build_up” candidate is expressed as a percent (1.13333%), while the “seasonal_trend” input is given as −0.075, which is a fraction (−7.5%), not −0.075%. Taking a weighted median/mean across candidates on different scales is invalid. If both were put on the same percent basis, the blended figure would land near 0.28%, not ~1.13%. Home Depot reports comparable sales as a year-over-year percent, so all components must be in percent before combining; as-is, the submitted 1.13333% rests on a wrong-scale aggregation.
2026-08-16T12:54:44Z  [HD] wrote submission\HD-FY2026Q2.xlsx
2026-08-16T12:54:44Z  [HD] wrote research\HD.md
2026-08-16T12:54:53Z    [HAS:Net fees] GATE critic: You applied the FY2024→FY2025 reported change (-12.68%, derived from 1,113.6 to 972.4 GBPm) as the FY2025→FY2026 growth rate to compute 972.4 × (1 − 12.68%) = 849.1. That’s a period error: the -12.68% pertains to FY2024→FY2025, not FY2025→FY2026. Without an FY2026-specific growth basis (guidance or consensus), reusing the prior year’s decline is the wrong period/basis for the forecast.
2026-08-16T12:55:15Z    [HAS:Pre-exceptional basic EPS] GATE critic: You derived 1.293p by plugging FY2025 P&L inputs (c. £45.09m operating profit, £13.4m net finance, 35.1% tax, 1,590.2m shares) into an EPS formula. Those figures align with FY2025 disclosures and reproduce c.1.29–1.31p, i.e., the reported FY2025 pre-exceptional EPS, not an FY2026 forecast. The result is for the wrong fiscal period.
2026-08-16T12:55:19Z    [DE:Production & Precision Ag operating profit] GATE critic: You overrode your own weighted blend (0.877×263.726 + 0.123×498.627 = 292.687 USDm) by submitting the lower candidate (263.726 USDm) via a “weighted median.” That’s a change of basis from the stated weighting scheme and effectively discards 12.3% of the evidence, pushing the estimate down to the lower model. The figure is therefore on the wrong aggregation basis relative to the inputs you presented.
