2026-08-16T12:56:14Z    [HAS:Pre-exceptional operating profit] GATE critic: You’ve anchored the FY2026 figure to a £45.2m “consensus” that appears to be a half‑year number, not a full‑year one. In the company’s own FY2025 disclosure, Pre-exceptional operating profit is c.£45.6m for a half-year versus £105.1m for the full year, which puts numbers in the ~£45m range squarely at the half-year scale. Using £45.2m as the full‑year FY2026 figure is therefore a wrong-period/scale error and likely about half of what a full‑year consensus would state.
